# Line-ending normalization: every text file is checked out as LF on all OSes.
#
# Why: Prettier is configured with endOfLine: "lf" (.prettierrc). On Windows,
# core.autocrlf=true produces CRLF working trees, so `pnpm format:check` fails
# locally even though CI (Linux, LF checkout) passes. eol=lf makes git check
# out LF everywhere, so local and CI checks agree.
#
# If you already have CRLF files in your working tree, refresh them with:
#   git add --renormalize . && git restore .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never EOL-normalize or apply diff/merge heuristics
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.bin binary
*.wasm binary
